  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find the missing side-lengths and angles for triangle $ABC$, given that. Give calculated lengths and angles correct to one decimal place:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$AB=3$, $BC=5$ and $\\angle BAC=50^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\angle ABC\\approx102.6^\\circ$, $\\angle ACB\\approx27.4^\\circ$, $AC\\approx6.4$.",
          "worked": "Using the sine rule,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin C&=\\frac{3\\sin50^\\circ}{5}\\\\C&\\approx27.4^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe supplementary angle is impossible because $152.6^\\circ+50^\\circ>180^\\circ$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}B&=180^\\circ-50^\\circ-C\\\\B&\\approx102.6^\\circ\\\\AC&=\\frac{5\\sin B}{\\sin50^\\circ}\\\\AC&\\approx6.4.\\end{align*}$$\n\nUnrounded values of $C$ and $B$ are used in subsequent calculations.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$AB=6$, $AC=4$ and $\\angle ACB=70^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\angle BAC\\approx71.2^\\circ$, $\\angle ABC\\approx38.8^\\circ$, $BC\\approx6.0$.",
          "worked": "Using the sine rule,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin B&=\\frac{4\\sin70^\\circ}{6}\\\\B&\\approx38.8^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe supplementary angle is impossible because $141.2^\\circ+70^\\circ>180^\\circ$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=180^\\circ-70^\\circ-B\\\\A&\\approx71.2^\\circ\\\\BC&=\\frac{6\\sin A}{\\sin70^\\circ}\\\\BC&\\approx6.0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nUnrounded values of $B$ and $A$ are used in subsequent calculations.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$BC=2$, $\\angle BAC=65^\\circ$ and $\\angle ABC=80^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\angle ACB=35^\\circ$, $AB\\approx1.3$, $AC\\approx2.2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}C&=180^\\circ-65^\\circ-80^\\circ\\\\C&=35^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing the sine rule,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}AB&=\\frac{2\\sin35^\\circ}{\\sin65^\\circ}\\\\AB&\\approx1.3\\\\AC&=\\frac{2\\sin80^\\circ}{\\sin65^\\circ}\\\\AC&\\approx2.2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
